{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: Calculus with Parametric Curves\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "##"
      ],
      "id": "c79b58ad"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| code-fold: true\n",
        "#| code-summary: Some plotting routines. Click to expand\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import sympy as sp\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "from sympy import plot_parametric, symbols\n",
        "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
        "from functools import partial\n",
        "\n",
        "## This is a 'partial function' so that we don't have to set figure size and aspect ratio every time.\n",
        "splot = partial(plot_parametric, aspect_ratio = (1,1),size=(4,4),axis_center = (0,0))\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def _plotter(x, y, create = False):\n",
        "    if create: plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
        "    plt.plot(x, y)\n",
        "    plt.gca().set_aspect('equal', adjustable='box')\n",
        "\n",
        "    return\n",
        "\n",
        "def _centeraxes():\n",
        "    ax = plt.gca()\n",
        "    # Move left y-axis and bottom x-axis to centre, passing through (0,0)\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax.spines['left'].set_position('zero')\n",
        "    ax.spines['bottom'].set_position('zero')\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Eliminate upper and right axes\n",
        "    ax.spines['right'].set_color('none')\n",
        "    ax.spines['top'].set_color('none')\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Show ticks in the left and lower axes only\n",
        "    ax.xaxis.set_ticks_position('bottom')\n",
        "    ax.yaxis.set_ticks_position('left')\n",
        "    return\n",
        "\n",
        "def _displayM(text, expr):\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  Display text and expression inline. \n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  display(Markdown('{} {}'.format(\n",
        "            text,\n",
        "            sp.latex(expr, mode='inline')\n",
        "          ))\n",
        "  )\n"
      ],
      "id": "7e9cc416",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Integration and Differentiation via python\n",
        "\n",
        "A quick reminder, you can perform differentiation and integration (definite or indefinite) as follows:"
      ],
      "id": "6a9e8030"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| code-summary: \"Sympy differentiate\"\n",
        "import sympy as sp\n",
        "x, y, z = sp.symbols('x y z')\n",
        "\n",
        "f = sp.cos(x)**3\n",
        "\n",
        "result = sp.diff(f)\n",
        "result\n",
        "## To evaluate a function, substitute the value of x.\n",
        "# result.subs(x,sp.pi/3)"
      ],
      "id": "c5892dfb",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| code-summary: \"Sympy integrate\"\n",
        "\n",
        "inf = sp.oo\n",
        "\n",
        "x, y, z = sp.symbols('x y z')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Indefinite integrals\n",
        "f = sp.ln(x)\n",
        "sp.integrate(f,x)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Definite integrals\n",
        "sp.integrate(sp.exp(-x), (x, 0, inf))"
      ],
      "id": "1f129252",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-caution collapse=\"true\" title=\"Warning\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "If integrate is unable to compute an integral, it returns an unevaluated Integral object.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tangents to Parametric Curves\n",
        "\n",
        "Steps:\n",
        "\n",
        "- For curve $C = (x(t), y(t))$, find $\\frac{dy}{dt}$ and $\\frac{dx}{dt}$.\n",
        "- Find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Example 1 (First derivative):\n",
        "*Find the tangent to the line $x = sec(t), y = tan(t)$ at $(\\sqrt(2),1)$ where $t=\\pi/4$.*"
      ],
      "id": "76b9afd3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "t = symbols('t')\n",
        "\n",
        "f = sp.sec(t)\n",
        "g = sp.tan(t)\n",
        "\n",
        "splot((f, g), (t, -sp.pi/3, sp.pi/3))"
      ],
      "id": "dfdcbd6c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Now we need to find the slope:"
      ],
      "id": "75ebc211"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "evalat = sp.pi/4\n",
        "\n",
        "dy_dx = sp.diff(g)/sp.diff(f)\n",
        "slope = dy_dx.subs(t, evalat)\n",
        "\n",
        "display(dy_dx)\n",
        "display(slope)"
      ],
      "id": "9ff965e9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "So our tangent is a line passing through $(\\sqrt{2},1)$ with slope `{python} slope`. Let's plot the curve and this tangent line together."
      ],
      "id": "02bec469"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# From question\n",
        "x0, y0 = sp.sqrt(2), 1\n",
        "\n",
        "## Parametric representation of a line\n",
        "x   = t\n",
        "y_t = slope * (t - x0) + y0\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plot both the curve and the tangent.\n",
        "splot((f, g,    (t, -sp.pi/3, sp.pi/3)), \n",
        "      (t, y_t,  (t, 0, 2)),\n",
        "      )"
      ],
      "id": "5b1a2ec1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Example 2 (Second derivatives):\n",
        "\n",
        " Find $\\frac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}$ as a function of $t$ if:\n",
        "$$\n",
        "x = t − t^2;\\quad y = t − t^3\n",
        "$$"
      ],
      "id": "9b3e2201"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paramterizations\n",
        "t = symbols('t')\n",
        "f = t - t**2\n",
        "g = t - t**3\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plot curve\n",
        "splot((f, g), (t, -1, 1.5))\n",
        "\n",
        "## Find first and second derivates to curve\n",
        "dy_dx = sp.diff(g)/sp.diff(f)\n",
        "d2y_dx = sp.simplify(sp.diff(dy_dx)/sp.diff(f))\n",
        "\n",
        "## Display resulting equations\n",
        "_displayM('First derivative:', dy_dx)\n",
        "_displayM('Second derivative:', d2y_dx)\n"
      ],
      "id": "9b72071e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Now we need to find the slope:"
      ],
      "id": "d3b08199"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "evalat = -0.75\n",
        "\n",
        "x0 = f.subs(t, evalat)\n",
        "y0 = g.subs(t, evalat)\n",
        "\n",
        "slope = dy_dx.subs(t, evalat)\n",
        "\n",
        "_displayM(f\"Slope at t = {evalat} is:\", slope)"
      ],
      "id": "ba4550c6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Let's replot the curve with the tangent."
      ],
      "id": "b03f142d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "x   = t\n",
        "y_t = slope * (t - x0) + y0\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plot both the curve and the tangent.\n",
        "splot((f, g,    (t, -sp.pi/3, sp.pi/3)), \n",
        "      (t, y_t,  (t, evalat - 1, evalat + 1)),\n",
        "      )"
      ],
      "id": "94de876d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Areas of Parametric Cruves\n",
        "\n",
        "### Example 3 (Area of astroid)\n"
      ],
      "id": "f947f130"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Paramterizations\n",
        "t = symbols('t')\n",
        "f = sp.cos(t)**3\n",
        "g = sp.sin(t)**3\n",
        "\n",
        "## Plot curve\n",
        "splot((f, g), (t, 0, 2* sp.pi))\n",
        "\n",
        "## Find first and second derivates to curve\n",
        "dy_dx = sp.diff(g)/sp.diff(f)\n",
        "d2y_dx = sp.simplify(sp.diff(dy_dx)/sp.diff(f))\n",
        "\n",
        "## Display resulting equations\n",
        "_displayM('First derivative:', dy_dx)\n",
        "_displayM('Second derivative:', d2y_dx)\n"
      ],
      "id": "bc896797",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "To find the area we make use of the symmetry of the object. We integrate $y$ from $x=[0,1]$ and multiply it by 4:\n"
      ],
      "id": "ee7f10d1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dx = sp.diff(f, t)\n",
        "y = g\n",
        "_displayM(\"Integrand:\", y*dx)\n",
        "\n",
        "sp.integrate(4*y*dx, (t, sp.pi/2, 0))"
      ],
      "id": "bb5d1633",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Length of Parametric Curves"
      ],
      "id": "7ec7aa1c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "marker = {\"color\": \"r\", \"marker\": \"s\", \"fillstyle\":'full',\"markerfacecolor\":'white', \"markersize\":3, \"linestyle\":'--'}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "t = sp.symbols('t')\n",
        "f = t**2\n",
        "g = sp.cos(50* t)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Evaluate functions at ten points \n",
        "numpoints = 10\n",
        "tval = [i/numpoints for i in list(range(0,numpoints))] + [1]\n",
        "fvals = [f.subs(t, t0 ) for t0 in tval]\n",
        "gvals = [g.subs(t, t0 ) for t0 in tval]\n",
        "marker[\"args\"] = [fvals,gvals]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plot parameters\n",
        "sp.plot_parametric(f,g, (t, 0, 1), markers = marker)\n"
      ],
      "id": "d398e330",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "$$\n",
        "L = \\int_a^b\\sqrt{f'(t)^2 + g'(t)^2} dt\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "To make things convenient we will convert our operations into a function."
      ],
      "id": "7814b61b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def _curvelength(f, g, var):\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  Inputs:\n",
        "    f, g: x and y parametrizations\n",
        "    var (tuple): (sp.symbol, lower lim, upper lim)\n",
        "\n",
        "    var is a  the variable upon which to integrate.\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  t, a, b = var\n",
        "\n",
        "  dx_dt = sp.diff(f, t)\n",
        "  dy_dt = sp.diff(g, t)\n",
        "\n",
        "  integ = (dx_dt**2 + dy_dt**2)\n",
        "  integ = sp.sqrt(integ)\n",
        "  _displayM(\"Integrating: \", integ)\n",
        "  _displayM(f\"over [{a}, {b}] w.r.t.\", t)\n",
        "\n",
        "  res = sp.integrate(integ, (t, a, b))\n",
        "  print(\"gives:\")\n",
        "\n",
        "  return res"
      ],
      "id": "351f8dd7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Example (circle/spiral)"
      ],
      "id": "3f5b71c8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "t, r = sp.symbols('t r', positive = True)\n",
        "\n",
        "f = r * sp.cos(t)\n",
        "g = r * sp.sin(t)\n",
        "\n",
        "_curvelength(f,g, (t, 0, 2 * sp.pi))"
      ],
      "id": "dc6dd0d2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Example (astroid)\n"
      ],
      "id": "f301e95a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "t = sp.symbols('t')\n",
        "\n",
        "f = (sp.cos(t))**3\n",
        "g = (sp.sin(t))**3\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "_curvelength(f,g, (t, 0, sp.pi/2))\n"
      ],
      "id": "2ceaf9e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Example (ellipse)"
      ],
      "id": "4250b811"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "t, a, b = sp.symbols('t a b', positive=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "f = a * sp.cos(t)\n",
        "g = b * sp.sin(t)\n",
        "\n",
        "_curvelength(f, g, (t, 0, sp.pi/2))"
      ],
      "id": "42969741",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This is a special integral called the _complete elliptic integral of the second kind_.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-note collapse=\"true\" title=\"Elliptic Integrals\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "[Elliptic integrals](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elliptic_integral)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's take the parametrization again and look for a series solution."
      ],
      "id": "206e6915"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dx_dt = sp.diff(f,t)\n",
        "dy_dt = sp.diff(g,t)\n",
        "\n",
        "ecc = sp.symbols('e')\n",
        "# e = sp.sqrt(1 - (b/a)**2)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "integrand = (dx_dt**2 + dy_dt**2)\n",
        "integrand = integrand.subs({a: b/sp.sqrt(1-ecc**2),\n",
        "                            sp.cos(t)**2: 1 - sp.sin(t**2)})\n",
        "integrand"
      ],
      "id": "30470b20",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "t, e = sp.symbols('t e')\n",
        "f = sp.sqrt(1 - e**2 * sp.sin(t**2))\n",
        "sp.series(f,t)\n"
      ],
      "id": "af7a85f0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
  ],
